| `shell.no_scripts` | string or null | `<project_slug> ships no shell script or shell test yet. Set this to null when it adds its first.`: `my_project ships no shell script or shell test yet. Set this to null when it adds its first.` by default; keel states that its gates are Python scripts | `null`, or a non-blank reason | `scripts/shell_gate.py`, through `scripts/config_loader.py`'s `shell.no_scripts` row | States why the project has no shell script and no shell test. With `shell.enabled` true and no shell file, every shell target is exit 13 (`NOTHING_JUDGED`) while this is `null`, because a pass over zero files proves nothing; with a reason, each target prints `shell.no_scripts says why (<reason>)` on stdout and exits 0 having run no tool. A reason left in place once a shell script or test exists is exit 14 naming the files, so the reason cannot outlive its truth; a blank reason is exit 14. Absent, the key is `null` and the targets write `[using default] shell.no_scripts = null` to stderr. | turning the shell gates off: `shell.enabled` | always |
